WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.701
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.100
You're here. You made it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:07.601
Thank you for tuning in.

00:00:07.601 --> 00:00:09.934
Well, guys, everyone is
talking about this.

00:00:09.934 --> 00:00:12.000
One of the biggest
events of the year --

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.868
the new Taylor Swift Eras movie
opened today in Los Angeles,

00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:20.133
and it premiered to thousands
of fans at a giant mall.

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:21.767
Yeah, that's how
powerful Taylor is.

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:24.467
In 2023, she can get people
to a mall.

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:26.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.767 --> 00:00:29.400
Yep. Right now, the friendship
bracelet section at Claire's

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.267
looks like a Walmart
on Black Friday.

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:34.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.467
Yep, Taylor's movie is expected
to have the biggest opening

00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:41.334
ever for a concert film
and could make $200 million.

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:45.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:48.067
At this point,
the United States is essentially

00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:49.667
a Taylor Swift-based economy.

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:51.534
[ Laughter, cheers ]

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:53.334
But theaters are encouraging
everyone

00:00:53.334 --> 00:00:56.767
who goes to the movie to sing,
dance, and take selfies.

00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:59.033
It's a real experience.
The movie is so popular,

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:00.601
they're going to have to
start showing it in stadiums,

00:01:00.601 --> 00:01:01.834
and it's going to be called

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:04.734
Taylor Swift The Eras Tour
The Movie The Tour.

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:06.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:08.000
Well, let's get to some news.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Congressman Jorge Santos
was just hit

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.567
with 10 more criminal charges
that accused him of stealing

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:16.400
his donors' identities
and credit cards.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.868
Santos was like, "Wait.
Am I not Henrietta Ellenburg,

00:01:20.868 --> 00:01:23.467
from Youngstown, Ohio?"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:25.234
It's wild.
Santos is either gonna wind up

00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:27.067
as Trump's running mate
or Trump's cellmate.

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:29.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.534 --> 00:01:31.868
Yeah, it's not looking good
for Santos.

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:35.000
In his defense, his lawyer just
posted the Kevin James meme.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.067
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.067 --> 00:01:40.467
-Some more news from Washington.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.801
This morning,
during a closed-door meeting,

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:45.200
Republicans nominated
Steve Scalise

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.234
to be the next
speaker of the House.

00:01:47.234 --> 00:01:48.801
And during the meeting,
congressmen were encouraged

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:50.467
to sing, dance,
and take selfies.

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:52.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.267
Yep, Steve Scalise
was nominated,

00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:55.601
and then Jorge Santos
was like,

00:01:55.601 --> 00:01:56.767
"Thank you. I accept.
Thank you."

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:58.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.367
Well, switching gears,

00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:02.501
Amazon Prime Day
started yesterday,

00:02:02.501 --> 00:02:04.334
and I read that Amazon
has actually been trying

00:02:04.334 --> 00:02:06.734
to crack down
on fake product reviews,

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:09.767
but luckily you can usually
tell when a review is fake.

00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:12.033
For instance, here's
a pack of Necco Wafers.

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:13.400
The fake review says...

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.200
Can't be real.
The real review says...

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:23.501
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, that's terrible.

00:02:23.501 --> 00:02:24.968
-See what I'm saying?
You can tell.

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:29.167
[ Applause ]

00:02:29.167 --> 00:02:32.601
Next up, here's a little model
BMW toy car.

00:02:32.601 --> 00:02:33.767
Fake review says...

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:36.801
The real one says...

00:02:38.701 --> 00:02:42.033
[ Laughter and applause ]
7 years old.

00:02:42.033 --> 00:02:45.200
Here's a Darth Vader
Echo Dot speaker.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.434
The fake review says...

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:50.334
The real one says...

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:55.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:58.300
-[ Imitating Darth Vader
breathing ]

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:01.300
-Next up, here's a 14-foot
garage freezer.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:02.634
Fake reviews says...

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:05.767
Real one says...

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:11.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:13.534
Two bodies...

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:16.067
Next up,
here's a full body pillow.

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:17.934
-Oh.
-Yeah, the fake review says...

00:03:19.334 --> 00:03:20.667
A real one says...

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:27.701
[ Laughter, audience groans ]

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:29.667
Dustin and Susan.
-That's the real review.

00:03:29.667 --> 00:03:31.534
-That's the real one.
That's the -- correct.

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:34.934
Yep. Next, here's the 3-in-1
sports center for kids.

00:03:34.934 --> 00:03:36.100
Yeah. A fake review says...

00:03:39.267 --> 00:03:40.534
Real one says...

00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:47.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:50.734
And finally, here's a
brain-shaped Jell-O mold.

00:03:50.734 --> 00:03:52.033
Fake reviews says...

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.467
Real one says...

00:03:57.367 --> 00:04:00.100
Yeah. See?
Now you can trust the review.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:01.934
Yeah.
[ Applause ]

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:04.067
Hey, guys, listen to this.
According to a new report,

00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:06.534
NASA believes that, by 2040,

00:04:06.534 --> 00:04:09.334
Americans will be living
in houses on the Moon.

00:04:09.334 --> 00:04:10.801
-Yeah.
-Nice.

00:04:10.801 --> 00:04:13.067
-And you thought it was tough
getting your friends to visit

00:04:13.067 --> 00:04:14.300
after you moved
to the suburbs.

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:16.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.334 --> 00:04:19.033
Yeah, we're just two decades
away from an HGTV show

00:04:19.033 --> 00:04:21.267
where someone's like, "I love
the schools in this crater,

00:04:21.267 --> 00:04:23.200
but I just hate
the kitchen countertops."

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:24.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.501 --> 00:04:27.367
Some business news.
Today, Birkenstock went public

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:31.033
at a valuation of $8 billion.
-Ooh.

00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:32.968
-When they rang the bell
at the New York Stock Exchange,

00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:34.534
the bell was like, "Ugh!"

00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:36.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.868 --> 00:04:40.067
[ Cymbals crash ]

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:42.701
"Need to take a shower,
and then I'll be good."

00:04:42.701 --> 00:04:44.300
Actually,
'cause it's Birkenstock,

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.467
they didn't ring
the opening bell,

00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:47.000
they just drummed
the opening bongo.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:51.400
Well, get this -- the prize
for tonight's Powerball drawing

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:54.534
is over $1.7 billion,

00:04:54.534 --> 00:04:57.400
the second-biggest jackpot
in lottery history.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.934
-And I already got my numbers
locked and loaded, Jimmy.

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:01.567
Let's go.
-Oh, really?

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.300
I didn't even know you played
Powerball, Kamal.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.234
Good luck.
-First number's 66, man.

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:08.033
That's the date
I met my wife, June 6th.

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:09.701
Boom.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:05:09.701 --> 00:05:11.100
-That's really sweet.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:15.033
-Next number's 20.
We've been married 20 years.

00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:16.300
-20 years.
Congratulations, bud.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:17.901
Thanks, man. Thanks.
It feels good.

00:05:17.901 --> 00:05:20.501
My next number, 24.

00:05:20.501 --> 00:05:21.968
That's how many times
my wife told me

00:05:21.968 --> 00:05:25.100
not to spend the whole paycheck
on lottery tickets.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:26.567
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, maybe don't spend

00:05:26.567 --> 00:05:27.834
the whole paycheck on it.

00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:29.701
-And then there's 25.
That's the number of times

00:05:29.701 --> 00:05:32.267
I told my wife
we need to win the Powerball

00:05:32.267 --> 00:05:34.968
'cause I just bought us a pair
of Jet Skis that I want to ride

00:05:34.968 --> 00:05:37.167
at the same time,
like the Little Mermaid's dad

00:05:37.167 --> 00:05:39.167
riding a pair of dolphins.

00:05:39.167 --> 00:05:41.400
You ever ride a dolphin,
J roll?

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:43.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.167 --> 00:05:45.501
-No, I can't say
I ever have.

00:05:45.501 --> 00:05:48.100
What's the next number?
-3.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:50.133
My wife hasn't returned
my texts in three days.

00:05:50.133 --> 00:05:51.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:53.901
Even when she does, it's usually
something like,

00:05:53.901 --> 00:05:56.801
"I guess," or "K."

00:05:56.801 --> 00:05:58.133
-That doesn't sound good.

00:05:58.133 --> 00:06:00.434
Finally, what's
your Powerball number?

00:06:00.434 --> 00:06:04.067
-6. 'Cause I'm staying
at a Motel 6 tonight.

00:06:04.067 --> 00:06:06.067
Continental breakfast, baby!

00:06:06.067 --> 00:06:07.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:07.267 --> 00:06:09.067
Unless -- Unless, Jimmy,

00:06:09.067 --> 00:06:10.701
still got that
guest bedroom at your place?

00:06:10.701 --> 00:06:12.501
I'd love to crash there.
-Kamal Gray, everybody.

00:06:12.501 --> 00:06:13.968
Good luck at the Powerball,
Kamal.

00:06:13.968 --> 00:06:15.300
I hope you win.

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:18.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:20.767 --> 00:06:22.200
-Hey, guys,
I saw that to avoid

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:25.033
repeating last year's holiday
travel meltdown,

00:06:25.033 --> 00:06:27.634
Southwest Airlines is stepping
up their preparation

00:06:27.634 --> 00:06:29.400
for the winter now.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:30.968
Yep, they're very prepared.

00:06:30.968 --> 00:06:32.767
They've already had
300 texts drafted

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:35.167
that say,
"Your flight is canceled."

00:06:35.167 --> 00:06:37.601
All you have to do
is hit send.

00:06:37.601 --> 00:06:39.601
Guys, I heard about a dog
in Michigan

00:06:39.601 --> 00:06:41.267
that was rescued
after getting his head

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:43.567
stuck in a plastic
cheese-ball container.

00:06:43.567 --> 00:06:44.901
Look at this.

00:06:44.901 --> 00:06:46.667
-Aww.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:47.834
-That will basically be
everyone's pet

00:06:47.834 --> 00:06:50.300
when we're living on the Moon.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:51.567
After getting his head out,

00:06:51.567 --> 00:06:53.100
he was like, "Wait. Is that
cheese powder in there?"

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:55.100
and got it stuck in there again.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:57.601
Guys, it's time for
"Good News, Bad News."

00:06:57.601 --> 00:06:59.267
First up, the good news --

00:06:59.267 --> 00:07:02.334
"Taylor Swift: The Eras Tour"
hit theaters this weekend.

00:07:02.334 --> 00:07:05.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:06.934
Bad news is, Lauren Boebert

00:07:06.934 --> 00:07:08.534
and her date reserved
the seats right next to you.

00:07:08.534 --> 00:07:10.601
[ Audience groans ]
Yeah.

00:07:10.601 --> 00:07:12.300
The good news is,
Biden is trying

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:14.200
to ban hidden junk fees.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.968
The bad news is, you got fired
for Googling

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:17.267
"hidden junk"
on your work computer.

00:07:17.267 --> 00:07:19.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:21.167
Here's some good news.

00:07:21.167 --> 00:07:24.901
Alaska Airlines is making
its own custom-blend coffee.

00:07:24.901 --> 00:07:26.334
The bad news,
Spirit Airlines

00:07:26.334 --> 00:07:28.667
is continuing to bootleg
its own moonshine.

00:07:28.667 --> 00:07:32.167
[ Laughter ]

00:07:32.167 --> 00:07:33.968
The good news is,
Chip and Joanna Gaines

00:07:33.968 --> 00:07:35.734
are launching a podcast.

00:07:35.734 --> 00:07:37.400
The bad news is, if you take
a drink every time

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:38.934
they say "shiplap,"
you'll black out.

00:07:38.934 --> 00:07:41.701
[ Laughter ]

00:07:41.701 --> 00:07:43.133
Up next, some good news.

00:07:43.133 --> 00:07:46.734
California has banned a type
of artificial red dye in food.

00:07:46.734 --> 00:07:48.334
-Whoo!
-Yep. Bad news is,

00:07:48.334 --> 00:07:50.501
the Kool-Aid Man
was just like, "Oh, nooo!"

00:07:50.501 --> 00:07:55.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.167
The good news is, Panda Express
is now offering dessert.

00:07:58.167 --> 00:08:00.067
-Ooh!
[ Scattered cheers ]

00:08:00.067 --> 00:08:01.968
-The bad news is, Panda Express
is now offering dessert.

00:08:01.968 --> 00:08:05.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:05.634 --> 00:08:07.467
Maybe I should give you
the bad news first, right?

00:08:07.467 --> 00:08:09.234
That might be better.
All right, here we go. Yeah.

00:08:09.234 --> 00:08:11.133
The bad news is,
Paris is reeling

00:08:11.133 --> 00:08:13.834
from a bedbug infestation.

00:08:13.834 --> 00:08:15.534
Good news is,
Pixar is making a movie

00:08:15.534 --> 00:08:17.100
where a French bedbug
runs a hotel.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:18.534
[ Laughter ]

00:08:18.534 --> 00:08:20.334
I'd watch that.
-Oui, oui!

00:08:20.334 --> 00:08:22.367
-[ French accent ]
Welcome to a bed!

00:08:22.367 --> 00:08:23.834
[ Normal voice ]
Next, the bad news,

00:08:23.834 --> 00:08:26.801
the new iPhone 15
has been overheating.

00:08:26.801 --> 00:08:28.701
The good news is that burnt hand
is still better

00:08:28.701 --> 00:08:30.734
than green texts
in the group chat.

00:08:30.734 --> 00:08:33.133
[ Laughter ]

00:08:33.133 --> 00:08:34.434
Next up, the bad news --

00:08:34.434 --> 00:08:36.167
edible cookie dough
is being recalled

00:08:36.167 --> 00:08:38.968
for containing
an undeclared allergen.

00:08:38.968 --> 00:08:40.801
The good news is, warning
about eating raw cookie

00:08:40.801 --> 00:08:42.167
dough never stopped you before.

00:08:42.167 --> 00:08:45.567
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:08:45.567 --> 00:08:47.534
And, finally, the bad news.

00:08:47.534 --> 00:08:51.300
Trump and Biden appear to be
heading for a rematch in 2024.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:52.868
[ Audience groans ]
Good news is, the loser

00:08:52.868 --> 00:08:55.033
gets to star in the next season
of "The Golden Bachelor."

00:08:55.033 --> 00:08:57.601
There you go.
That would work.

00:08:57.601 --> 00:08:58.767
I'll watch that.

00:08:58.767 --> 00:09:02.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:02.434 --> 00:09:05.300
And, finally, everyone's still
talking about Taylor Swift

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:07.334
and Travis Kelce and --

00:09:07.334 --> 00:09:09.067
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah. Why not?

00:09:09.067 --> 00:09:11.033
I know.
We love them both,

00:09:11.033 --> 00:09:13.400
but the relationship
has united two groups

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:17.667
that don't normally hang out --
Taylor Swift fans and NFL fans.

00:09:17.667 --> 00:09:19.434
Well, we wanted to test
their knowledge of each other,

00:09:19.434 --> 00:09:21.133
so we went down
to 30 Rock Plaza

00:09:21.133 --> 00:09:22.634
